We need answer only JSON object. Need solve PLC task, use tools compile/simulate/verify max limits. Need save final candidate.json. But filesystem read-only sandbox? Shell commands unnecessary per user; tools supplied. We need create candidate.json — filesystem restricted read-only, cannot write via shell likely. Maybe MCP tool writes? Instructions say save exact final submitted source to candidate.json. We can perhaps apply_patch? Only shell tool available, read-only. Hmm. There is no apply_patch tool exposed! Tools are shell_command and MCP. We can try shell to write but sandbox read-only and approval never. Yet perhaps task expects tool calls and candidate.json via shell? Need see cwd. We must not inspect other dirs. We can inspect current workspace only perhaps. User says shell commands unnecessary. We should use PLC tools directly.

First understand desired ST. FB_Task initial Run=false, ResetRequired=true. Inputs Start Stop EStopNC Reset BOOL; outputs Run ResetRequired BOOL. Need implement behavior priority EStop > ResetRequired > Stop > Start. Careful pre-state semantics: outputs retained from previous scan cannot initialize FB outputs to TRUE/FALSE in declaration? In CODESYS, can set initial value in VAR_OUTPUT: `Run : BOOL := FALSE; ResetRequired : BOOL := TRUE;`. That establishes pre-state. Scan executes once.

Logic:
IF NOT EStopNC THEN
    ResetRequired := TRUE;
    Run := FALSE;
ELSIF ResetRequired THEN
    Run := FALSE;
    IF Reset AND NOT Start AND NOT Stop THEN
        ResetRequired := FALSE;
    END_IF;
ELSE
    IF Stop THEN
        Run := FALSE;
    ELSIF Start THEN
        Run := TRUE;
    END_IF;
END_IF;

ValidReset in LTL is EStopNC & Reset & !Start & !Stop. In requirement, while ResetRequired TRUE, only clears when Reset = TRUE AND Start = FALSE AND Stop = FALSE; EStop? Priority says E-stop > ResetRequired, so only reset if EStop healthy, implied by reaching the ELSIF ResetRequired branch (EStopNC true). Indeed validReset includes EStopNC. Good.

P3 G(qRequired -> !Run) — if qRequired true (previous output ResetRequired), Run must be false. Our branch ELSIF ResetRequired (since outputs retain prev) sets Run false even when EStop false too. Good. P4 G((qRequired & EStopNC) -> (ResetRequired <-> !validReset)). When qRequired true, EStop true: ResetRequired must be true iff invalid reset. Our logic: ResetRequired set FALSE if valid reset; remains true otherwise. Yes. P7 if !qRequired & EStopNC -> !ResetRequired. Our logic: if qRequired false, EStop true, else branch? Careful after ELSIF: if ResetRequired false, goes ELSE and does not alter ResetRequired, remains false. P7 true. P5 etc. Good.

Formal verify tool likely supports subset. Need compile. We need possibly formal verify requiring declaration named FB_Task and no initial output? Let's call compile with declaration string and implementation. Supporting_objects empty. We should use only 3 calls. First compile. Need maybe syntax: FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task VAR_INPUT ... END_VAR VAR_OUTPUT ... END_VAR. Output initial values syntax in CODESYS: `Run : BOOL := FALSE; ResetRequired : BOOL := TRUE;`. Good.

Need decide title etc. Use compile_st.

